    <h2>What is VIN Decoding?</h2>
    <p>VIN decoding is the process of translating a 17-character Vehicle Identification Number into readable vehicle information. Every vehicle manufactured after 1981 receives a unique VIN that acts as its automotive fingerprint. No two vehicles in operation share the same VIN.</p>
    <p>When you enter a VIN into our decoder, we query the official NHTSA Vehicle Product Information Catalog (VPIC) database to extract detailed specifications assigned during manufacturing. This includes the make, model, year, engine type, body style, drive type, transmission, plant of manufacture, and much more.</p>

    <h2>What Information Does a VIN Decode Reveal?</h2>
    <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 my-6">
